WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.720
"Benefits of Cumin and
Saffron for Weight Loss"

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.840
In my video, "Benefits of Black Cumin for
Weight Loss," a total of 17 randomized

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.720
controlled trials showed that
the simple spice could reduce

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:20.960
cholesterol and triglycerides.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.480
And the side effects?
A weight-loss effect.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.520
Saffron is another spice found
to be effective for treating

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.480
a major cause of suffering--
depression in this case--

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.120
with a side effect
of decreased appetite.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:36.960
When put to the test in a randomized,
double-blind, placebo-controlled trial,

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.120
saffron, indeed, was found to
lead to a significant weight loss:

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.560
five pounds more than placebo,

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.520
and an extra inch off
the waist in eight weeks.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:48.560
The dose of saffron used in
the study was the equivalent

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:53.120
of drinking a cup of tea made from
a large pinch of saffron threads.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:56.240
Suspecting the active ingredient
might be crocin,

00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:00.080
the pigment in saffron that
accounts for its crimson color,

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.680
researchers also tried giving people
just the purified pigment.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.560
That led to weight loss, too,
but it didn't do as well

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:08.560
as the full saffron extract,

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:11.760
beating the placebo by only
two pounds and half an inch.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.400
The mechanism appeared
to be appetite suppression,

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.200
as the crocin group ended up averaging
about 80 fewer calories a day,

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:26.160
whereas the full saffron group consumed
170 calories less a day on average.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.440
A similar study looked specifically
at snacking frequency.

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.320
The researchers thought perhaps
the mood-boosting effects of saffron

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:37.280
might cut down on stress-related eating.
Indeed, eight weeks of a saffron extract

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.440
did cut snack intake in half, compared
to placebo, accompanied by

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.120
a slight but statistically significant
weight loss, about two pounds.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:50.000
Even the loss of a few pounds is pretty
remarkable given the tiny doses utilized,

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.080
about 100 mg, which is equivalent

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:56.160
to about an eighth of
a teaspoon of the spice.

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:02.320
The problem is that saffron is the
most expensive spice in the world.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.720
It's composed of delicate
threads sticking up out of

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:06.720
the saffron crocus flower.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:11.680
Each flower produces only a few
threads, so you'd need 50,000 flowers

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:15.840
to make a single pound of spice--
enough flowers to cover a football field.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:20.480
So that pinch of saffron
could cost a dollar a day.

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:24.640
That's why in my 21 tweaks to accelerate
weight loss in "How Not to Diet,"

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.600
instead of saffron,
I include black cumin,

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:33.000
which at a quarter teaspoon a day
would only cost three cents a day.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.800
But what about just regular cumin?

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.640
Used in cuisines around the world
from Tex-Mex to South Asian,

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.960
cumin is the second most popular
spice on Earth after black pepper.

00:02:44.960 --> 00:02:47.280
It's one of the oldest
cultivated plants with a range

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:49.120
of purported medicinal uses,

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:54.000
but only recently has it been
put to the test for weight loss.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.760
Those randomized
to a half teaspoon

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.360
at both lunch and dinner
over three months

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.360
lost about four more pounds
and an extra inch off their waist.

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:07.280
The spice was found comparable
to the obesity drug known as orlistat.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:10.640
For those of you who don't remember,
that's the "anal leakage" drug

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:14.720
you may have heard about, sold under
the brand names Alli and Xenical,

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:17.360
though the drug company
apparently prefers the term

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:22.160
"faecal spotting" to describe
the rectal discharge it causes.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:25.920
The drug company's website
offered some helpful tips, though.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:31.440
"It's probably a smart idea
to wear dark pants,

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:34.320
and bring a change of
clothes with you to work."

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:39.840
You know, just in case their drug
causes you to crap your pants at work.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:45.266
I think I'll stick with the cumin,
thank you very much.

